// ── Spec-consistency hook snippet ───────────────────────────────────────────
//
// MERGE this into .claude/settings.json (don't paste the file wholesale — your
// settings.json already has permissions/model/other hooks; only add the entry
// under the "hooks" key). This makes the MECHANICAL spec controls fire
// deterministically when Claude edits a spec file, rather than relying on the
// agent remembering to run them.
//
// The principle (confirmed in the Claude Code docs): CLAUDE.md and agents are
// advisory; hooks are deterministic. The reviewer gates (C9-C11) stay with the
// agent/skill because they need judgement; the mechanical checks (C1-C4, C8)
// belong in a hook because they don't.
//
// PostToolUse fires AFTER an edit. The matcher restricts it to spec files so it
// doesn't run on every code edit. Adjust the matcher path to your repo if your
// specs live elsewhere than .claude/specs/.

{
  "hooks": {
    "PostToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Edit|Write",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "f=$(jq -r '.tool_input.file_path // empty'); case \"$f\" in *.claude/specs/*) out=$(bash \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/check-spec-consistency.sh\" 2>&1) || { echo \"$out\" >&2; exit 2; };; esac"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}

// NOTE: the exact env var carrying the edited path (read from stdin JSON via jq) and
// the PostToolUse schema can vary by Claude Code version. Verify against
// `code.claude.com/docs` → Configure settings → hooks for your installed
// version, and adjust the guard condition if the variable name differs. If in
// doubt, drop the `if echo ... grep` guard and let it run on every edit — the
// checker is fast and exits 0 when there are no service manifests yet.
